    "unresolvedReleaseQuestionCount": 9,
    "unresolvedReleaseQuestions": [
      {
        "trackId": "nd-dui-record-seal",
        "affectedElement": "governing_mechanism",
        "question": "N.D.C.C. § 39-08-01.6(1) says the court shall seal, and states no motion or petition trigger, whereas the neighbouring marijuana provision says expressly upon motion. The petition requirement therefore rests on the official ND Courts research guide rather than on the statutory text, and participant copy must not represent the petition as statutorily mandated."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "nd-dui-record-seal",
        "affectedElement": "eligibility_branch",
        "question": "The exclusion of impaired-driving offences from Chapter 12-60.1 appears only in the official ND Courts research guides and not in the statutory exclusions at N.D.C.C. § 12-60.1-02(2), which list only violence-or-intimidation felonies inside the firearm-disability period and registration offences. The routing to the separate § 39-08-01.6 seal follows the official guides, but the basis should be confirmed before release."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "nd-marijuana-first-offense-seal",
        "affectedElement": "legal_effect_or_warning",
        "question": "The official general expungement research guide describes this route as an expungement, while the statute says seal and the sealing guide treats it as sealing. The statute controls and participant copy must say seal, but the conflict between two official publications should be recorded."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "nd-marijuana-first-offense-seal",
        "affectedElement": "waiting_period",
        "question": "The two-year period has no anchor date on the face of the statute. The words are that the person is not subsequently convicted within two years of a further violation of this chapter, which is grammatically open between two years from the judgment and two years from the further violation. This is a genuine textual ambiguity rather than an unread statute, and it decides who qualifies."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "nd-seal-felony-conviction",
        "affectedElement": "eligibility_branch",
        "question": "The exclusion of impaired-driving offences from Chapter 12-60.1 appears only in the official ND Courts research guides and not in the statutory exclusions at N.D.C.C. § 12-60.1-02(2), which list only violence-or-intimidation felonies inside the firearm-disability period and registration offences. The routing to the separate § 39-08-01.6 seal follows the official guides, but the basis should be confirmed before release."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "nd-seal-felony-conviction",
        "affectedElement": "filing_process",
        "question": "The filing fee for a Chapter 12-60.1 petition is not established. The statewide court fee schedule effective 1 July 2025, compiled under N.D.C.C. § 27-05.2-03, carries no line item for this petition or for any motion within an existing criminal case, and the official research guide tells the participant to contact the clerk to confirm the amount, if any. No fee figure may be shown to a participant until a clerk-level answer is obtained."
      },
